    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours, which translates to 15° per hour or 1° every 4 minutes.",
        "Latitude measures distance North or South of the Equator (0°), while Longitude measures distance East or West of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is based on the 82°30' E longitude, passing near Prayagraj / Mirzapur.",
        "Time increases as you travel East from the Prime Meridian (+ GMT) and decreases as you travel West (- GMT).",
        "The International Date Line lies near the 180° meridian; crossing it eastward gains a day, while crossing westward loses a day."
      ],
      "id": "2rm48hd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "070ll4a",
      "content": "The Earth rotates from west to east. Because of this rotation, places to the east see the Sun earlier and their clocks show a later time. Places to the west see the Sun later and their clocks show an earlier time. This single concept is the key to solving all longitude–time numericals."
    },
    {
      "id": "nsv5xjr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FORMULAS WITH LOGIC"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ex5zsn",
      "content": "Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "emihitd",
      "content": "So, rotation per hour = 360° ÷ 24 = 15°."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wasynzj",
      "content": "This means: 15° longitude difference = 1 hour time difference. Further dividing:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9y8lluj",
      "content": "1° longitude = 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nzl04ra",
      "content": "Always remember: East → Add time | West → Subtract time."
    },
    {
      "id": "7zwxman",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v1suzf0",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "11dk7n4",
      "content": "What is the time difference between two places having a longitude difference of 30°?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "opzwmii",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tauel9n",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand what is given. Longitude difference = 30°. Step 2: Recall the basic rule: 15° longitude = 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n6bzqms",
      "content": "Step 3: Divide the longitude difference by 15. 30° ÷ 15° = 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h1tpuuh",
      "content": "Step 4: Since only time difference is asked, direction is not needed. Final Answer: Time difference is 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a36t7d1",
      "content": "Common Mistake: Students try to convert into minutes unnecessarily."
    },
    {
      "id": "6xo9615",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tjqkfan",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fjvmatw",
      "content": "Find the time difference for 1° longitude."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i7kepj3",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pp79nvy",
      "content": "Step 1: Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o1rb0y0",
      "content": "Step 2: Convert hours into minutes: 24 × 60 = 1440 minutes. Step 3: Divide total minutes by total degrees."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tdxp6bj",
      "content": "1440 ÷ 360 = 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d9v0bzg",
      "content": "Final Answer: 1° longitude corresponds to 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2puqyjf",
      "content": "Exam Tip: This is the MOST IMPORTANT value in SSC numericals."
    },
    {
      "id": "26m8rq2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o7g2k0u",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jkz444e",
      "content": "If the local time at Greenwich is 10:00 AM, what will be the local time at 30° East?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "frklpdk",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ske9o9j",
      "content": "Step 1: Identify reference point: Greenwich (0°). Step 2: Identify target longitude: 30° East."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g5uj9f5",
      "content": "Step 3: Calculate longitude difference = 30°. Step 4: Convert degrees into time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fry0or3",
      "content": "30° ÷ 15 = 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t1o98iz",
      "content": "Step 5: Decide direction. East means ahead in time. Step 6: Add time to Greenwich time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dz1q3cb",
      "content": "10:00 AM + 2 hours = 12:00 Noon. Final Answer: Local time = 12:00 PM."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dbzqlx4",
      "content": "Common Mistake: Students subtract instead of adding."
    },
    {
      "id": "zob72b0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k65nvnf",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "45ht7h5",
      "content": "If the local time at 45° West is 6:00 AM, what is the time at Greenwich?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zczk8te",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jemwi1w",
      "content": "Step 1: Identify given place: 45° West. Step 2: Greenwich is east of this place. Step 3: Longitude difference = 45°."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "631g1ps",
      "content": "Step 4: Convert into time. 45° ÷ 15 = 3 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tmituvf",
      "content": "Step 5: West is behind, so Greenwich time will be ahead. Step 6: Add time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w20mohz",
      "content": "6:00 AM + 3 hours = 9:00 AM."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6koakue",
      "content": "Final Answer: Greenwich time = 9:00 AM."
    },
