    {
      "id": "v2glasr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4e99ij3",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8gfhlds",
      "content": "When it is 12:00 noon GMT, what is the time in India (IST)?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hgbsx3e",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "82fifby",
      "content": "Step 1: Remember IST relation. IST = GMT + 5 hours 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o4zqf1g",
      "content": "Step 2: Add 5 hours 30 minutes to 12:00 noon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ue0tf7m",
      "content": "12:00 + 5:30 = 5:30 PM."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7j8kbwy",
      "content": "Final Answer: IST = 5:30 PM."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ybtkqw",
      "content": "Exam Tip: Never change date unless IDL is mentioned."
    },
    {
      "id": "57mhogk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p2ikcqd",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vxn5r9c",
      "content": "A place is located at 97½° East longitude. If the time at Greenwich is 6:00 AM, find the local time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w3zbvef",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ip7qk65",
      "content": "Step 1: Identify longitude difference = 97.5°. Step 2: Convert degrees to hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mshrhnx",
      "content": "97.5 ÷ 15 = 6.5 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cvv9y4o",
      "content": "Step 3: Convert decimal into minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "koz8n1j",
      "content": "0.5 hour = 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e673ay1",
      "content": "Step 4: Direction is East, so add time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wjn91h1",
      "content": "6:00 AM + 6 hours 30 minutes = 12:30 PM. Final Answer: Local time = 12:30 PM."
    },
    {
      "id": "6iz5t2z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Calculate time difference between two longitudes using 1° = 4 minutes.",
        "Remember that Indian Standard Time (82.5° E) is exactly 5 hours and 30 minutes ahead of GMT.",
        "Understand the difference between local time (based on sun position) and standard time (based on central meridian)."
      ],
      "id": "c1wmm03"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yywa04u",
      "content": "Question:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6bgshmi",
      "content": "A ship crosses the International Date Line from West to East on Monday. What will be the day?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6oc6wmc",
      "content": "Ultra Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zukoo15",
      "content": "Step 1: Recall IDL rule."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wczhc3c",
      "content": "West to East crossing means subtract one day. Step 2: Given day = Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ws6dzm",
      "content": "Step 3: Subtract one day. Monday − 1 = Sunday."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lb4mezq",
      "content": "Final Answer: Day will be Sunday."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lq45nog",
      "content": "Common Mistake: Students add a day incorrectly."
    },
    {
      "id": "v5ju5z0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FINAL EXAM STRATEGY"
    },
    {
      "id": "e35zyud",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "First convert longitude into time.",
        "Then decide direction (East/West).",
        "Only then add or subtract time.",
        "For IDL, change date separately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rqd7fsa",
      "content": "If this order is followed, mistakes will never happen."
    },
